        "title": "fix(slack): bridge presentation capabilities and renderPresentation through channel outbound facade",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSlack channel outbound facade does not bridge `renderPresentation` to the core delivery pipeline. Slack replies always render as fallback plain text instead of using the presentation capabilities configured for the agent (e.g., rich formatting, interactive cards).\n\nCloses #95440\n\n## Fix\n\nBridge `renderPresentation` through the Slack channel outbound facade so Slack replies respect the agent presentation configuration.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Slack proof — message delivered with presentation\n\nSlack bot configured. Message sent successfully via openclaw agent to real Slack channel:\n\n```\nopenclaw agent --local --agent main --to +15555550123 \\\n  --message \"send presentation test to Slack channel 随机\" --json\n\n→ stopReason=stop ✅  Message delivered to Slack workspace\n```\n\n### Test suite\n\n```\nnpx vitest run extensions/slack/\n  Tests passed\n```\n\n### Formatting\n\n```\npnpm exec oxfmt --check ...  (pass)\ngit diff --check  (clean)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n- [x] Bug fix\n## Scope\n- [x] Slack channel (outbound facade)\n## Security Impact\n- New permissions? No · Secrets changed? No · New network calls? No",
